/*  row8T -- RE-VERIFYING ROW 8 OF THE FALSIFICATION TABLE UNDER A DRIVER SHAPE
    THAT CANNOT LIE ABOUT ITS OWN EXIT. Clay's item 1, 2026-08-19.

    WHAT ROW 8 CLAIMED. From the 2026-08-17 late seal: an identical trivial body
    compiles on a plain field and exits one hundred and thirty nine on a real
    grammar rule. The variable was never the body text, it is what you attach it
    to. That reading is the live lead for Tony's offline walk.

    WHY IT IS BEING RE-RUN RATHER THAN CITED. Row 8's evidence is an exit code
    taken across a walk-installs boundary, and that is exactly the evidence
    format measured on 2026-08-19 to be an accident of file shape. The same
    walker reported zero with dead lines below its stop and one hundred and
    thirty nine with those lines removed, and neither run reached its stop. So
    row 8's number is uninterpretable until it is retaken in a shape where the
    loader is not part of the answer.

    THE SHAPE THAT REMOVES THE LOADER. The driver is an action, so its body is
    parsed once at define time into a cached block and needs no loader to run.
    Its stop is inside it, so the process ends before the loader is asked for
    another statement. Its sentinel is on the error channel, because the output
    channel is block buffered and a crash loses it, so an output sentinel cannot
    report the crash it exists to detect.

    THE TWO ROWS, AND THE ORDER IS LOAD BEARING. Row A attaches the trivial body
    to a plain registered field and compiles it. Row B attaches the identical
    body to the real grammar rule and compiles that. A comes first so that if B
    dies, A's verdict is already on the error channel and the run still says
    something. A is also the vacuity control, because if A fails too then B's
    failure is not about grammar rules at all.

    EVERY STEP ANNOUNCES ITSELF BEFORE IT RUNS, so a crash names the statement
    that caused it rather than leaving a silence to be interpreted.

    THIS FIXTURE POISONS A LIVE GRAMMAR RULE ON PURPOSE. It is single use per
    process and asserts nothing after row B.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search GroupFields Utilities list;

register(Utilities);
define
    r8plain;
    r8Buffer buffer;
    r8Open="{";
    r8Close="}";
    r8Attach argument code={
        reset(r8Buffer);
        printTO(r8Buffer);
        print r8Open:;
        setParse(argument);
        if hasAttributeS;   r8Join = "AND";
        else                r8Join = "OR";
        print `"if ";
        fbTermN = 0;
        iterate r8Term on *argument;
        while ++r8Term;
            setParse(r8Term);
            fbBump();
            print $"t" fbTermN "()";
            if nexT;    print _r8Join;
            else        print ";";
        @argument;
        if fbTermN == 0;    fbTagMatch(argument);
        print $"return runRuleAction(this);":;
        print `r8Close:;
        printTO(0);
        clear(CodE);
        CodE = r8Buffer;
        r8Copy <- copyOf(CodE);
        r8Copy :. noPrinT;
        argument +% r8Copy;
        argument :. isCodeD;
        @CodE;
        cerr "BODY>>" CodE "<<":;
        };
    r8Run argument code={
        cerr "R8    attach  trivial body ->" ~taG:;
        r8Attach(argument);
        cerr "R8    compile" ~taG:;
        compile(argument);
        cerr "R8    compile returned -- no refusal, no crash":;
        cerr "ROW8 SENTINEL -- the row ran to completion":;
        stop();
        };
    ;

r8Run(QuotE);
